From: Hariharan Basuthkar <hbasuthk@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:iw: fix HE40/EHT40 display on edge 6 GHz channels

The HE40 and EHT40 channel-width tokens were missing on the first and
last 6 GHz channels (e.g. 5955 MHz [1] and 7115 MHz [233]) in the
"iw phyxx channels" output.

The guard requires both NO_HT40_MINUS and NO_HT40_PLUS to be absent.
Edge channels have one direction blocked (no adjacent channel below or
above the band edge) but the other direction is valid. For 6 GHz HE,
40 MHz operation is available as long as at least one pairing direction
exists.

Fix by requiring only one direction to be clear (OR instead of AND),
matching the actual 40 MHz availability for these channels.

Feature: REGULATORY

Patch-dependency: 655-QSDK-PROTOCOL-iw-fix-6GHz-iftype-data-ordering-assumption.patch

Change-Id: I4594481fix2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d
Signed-off-by: Hariharan Basuthkar <hbasuthk@qti.qualcomm.com>
--- a/phy.c
+++ b/phy.c
@@ -265,12 +265,12 @@
 					if (ctx->width_160 && !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_160MHZ])
 						printf(" VHT160");
 					if (ctx->he_width_40 &&
-					    !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_MINUS] &&
-					    !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_PLUS])
+					    (!tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_MINUS] ||
+					     !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_PLUS]))
 						printf(" HE40");
 					if (ctx->eht_width_40 &&
-					    !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_MINUS] &&
-					    !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_PLUS])
+					    (!tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_MINUS] ||
+					     !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_HT40_PLUS]))
 						printf(" EHT40");
 					if (ctx->he_width_80 &&
 					    !tb_freq[NL80211_FREQUENCY_ATTR_NO_80MHZ])
